{"author":{"id":"2f242a7e7f2592f8909954a77fabece74f6e8cc197182647ed3b15ea8e3878af"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791138777,"nonce":"tB3M8CJieyafjoIlqjeM1/yotII=","message":"Root cause, from a trace through a patched winit: AppKit doesn't see an event posted while the run loop is blocked until the next display frame. Events posted before -[NSApplication run] starts are seen. winit stops every pump by posting from a run-loop observer, so a zero-timeout pump loops through cleared()/wakeup() (CSWS...) until a frame, or indefinitely when nothing else wakes the loop. A timed pump returns a frame late.\n\nFix in e505c4a3afd470c814973a267e2b8dc5b0982799:\n- A poll posts xwindow's own stop event (application-defined, subtype 0x7877, sequence number in data1) behind the queued events. A local event monitor calls -stop: when it dequeues the latest one and swallows every stop event. Polls no longer reach cleared(), so on macOS xwindow delivers requestRedraw itself.\n- A wait keeps the one-shot alarm from 0f0c735.\n- window_open uses a 1 ms pass on macOS, because a poll no longer runs winit's loop far enough to make a window.\n\nBench, empty window, wait 0.008 followed by one poll (external 75 Hz display): before 97% CPU, polls about 13 ms; after 5% CPU, empty poll 0.05 ms, wait lateness about 1 ms. Plain wait 0.008: 116 waits/s, 4% CPU.\n\nhlwindow e6b2fca pins it.","files":null}]}